  ('vocabulary', 'hard', 'multiple_choice', 'The lawyer offered a cogent argument supported by reliable records.', 'Which phrase could replace "cogent" without changing the main meaning?', 'Which phrase could replace "cogent" without changing the main meaning?', '[{"label":"A","text":"clear, logical, and convincing"},{"label":"B","text":"very attentive to accuracy and detail"},{"label":"C","text":"apparently, though perhaps not actually"},{"label":"D","text":"present or found everywhere"}]', 'A', 'In this context, "cogent" means "clear, logical, and convincing." The surrounding details support that meaning.', 'published', '{"stimulus_type":"text","blueprint":"context-meaning-4"}', '0dde605e66ce37c64e32e36ddaa59c70ac17a702e64b6fb916bbf419a803d33c', 'english-bank-2000-v2', '{"generator":"scripts/generate-question-bank.mjs","version":"2.0.0","blueprint":"context-meaning-4","ordinal":86,"locale":"en"}', 'english-bank:vocabulary:hard:086'),
  ('vocabulary', 'hard', 'multiple_choice', 'Balancing lower prices with fair wages created a conundrum.', 'Which phrase could replace "conundrum" without changing the main meaning?', 'Which phrase could replace "conundrum" without changing the main meaning?', '[{"label":"A","text":"unable to be changed"},{"label":"B","text":"a difficult problem with no obvious solution"},{"label":"C","text":"seemingly contradictory yet possibly true"},{"label":"D","text":"show that someone or something was right"}]', 'B', 'In this context, "conundrum" means "a difficult problem with no obvious solution." The surrounding details support that meaning.', 'published', '{"stimulus_type":"text","blueprint":"context-meaning-4"}', '83f32e088aedfc9173f185095820aa8808ce05d8c8daa48300a3c7d67ee148dd', 'english-bank-2000-v2', '{"generator":"scripts/generate-question-bank.mjs","version":"2.0.0","blueprint":"context-meaning-4","ordinal":87,"locale":"en"}', 'english-bank:vocabulary:hard:087'),
